// endpoint_register_repository.proto — RegisterRepository: a repository joins
// the roster ON ITS OWN, with no workspace. SIDEBAR section.
//
// It exists because a repository had exactly one way in: as a SIDE EFFECT of
// RegisterWorkspace, which mints the repository record for the worktree it is
// announcing. So the only way to make a repository pickable — for the static
// create, which is the one mode that names a repository by hand — was to
// register a workspace in it first, and there was no way at all to say "this
// repository exists" about a checkout nobody is working in yet.
//
// THE PATH IS ANY PATH INSIDE THE REPOSITORY, a file as readily as a
// directory, because that is what the caller HAS: the editor's gesture is
// "pick a file", and the repository is derived from it. The daemon resolves
// the repository's MAIN WORKTREE from that path through git — which is what
// workspace.v1's RepositoryRef.dir means — and normalizes it exactly as
// RegisterWorkspace normalizes a worktree dir.
//
// IDEMPOTENT BY THE RESOLVED DIR, and the answer SAYS SO rather than hiding
// it: `already_known` distinguishes "this is new" from "you already had it",
// which is the whole difference the caller reports to the user. Neither is an
// error.
//
// NOT PER-WORKSPACE. There is no ref to key on, so none of the ownership or
// handover arms applies — the same reason RegisterWorkspace carries none.

